<!-- Part 14 e2e scenario 4/5: three-level recursive containment
     (PumpType -> Drive -> Motor -> {Temperature, Readings}) with mixed
     ModellingRules and a non-default ValueRank, exercising recursive
     Effective Declaration Tree traversal together with §16-18 in
     combination, and the need-based design's central point: Drive/Motor
     are plain Object declarations with no local extension of their own, so
     neither gets a Virtual Type at all.

     Expect:
       PumpType   : hasDrive allValuesFrom/minQualifiedCardinality(1) DriveType directly (no VT)
       DriveType  : hasMotor allValuesFrom/minQualifiedCardinality(1) MotorType directly (no VT)
       MotorType  : hasTemperature allValuesFrom VT(MotorType,"Temperature"), no cardinality (Optional):
                     VT subClassOf PropertyType, ValueRank_Scalar (default), Datatype->Double
                  : hasReadings allValuesFrom/minQualifiedCardinality(1) VT(MotorType,"Readings")
                     (array Property, Mandatory): VT subClassOf PropertyType,
                     ValueRank_OneDimension (explicit), Datatype->Int32
     Temperature/Readings are Variables, so they always get their own VT (to
     carry ValueRank/Datatype), unlike the purely-structural Drive/Motor
     Object declarations above them. -->
